    <string name="privacy_policy_title">Privacy policy</string>
    <string name="privacy_policy_body">Revision date: 27 November 2026.\n\nnimWifi is a personal, open-source project by mpedreira, based on WiProber by htechno (MIT License). It has no accounts, advertising, analytics or developer server: nothing is collected by the author.\n\nSurveys: the app processes Wi-Fi network names and identifiers (SSID, BSSID), signal level, frequencies and security capabilities provided by Android. Projects (points and routes you mark, floor plans, notes, photos, imported ESX files and test results) stay in private storage until you delete them or clear the app\'s data. Projects may be included in Android\'s backup, depending on your device settings.\n\nAndroid requires the location permission to return Wi-Fi scan results. nimWifi never reads GPS coordinates.\n\nImported configuration and credentials stay in private storage, excluded from backups; credentials are never shown or exported, and those in a .har recording are removed on import.\n\nNetwork: nothing is sent unless you enable a test or import a configuration. Then the app connects over Wi-Fi only to the servers you configured and, for the default Internet speed test, to speed.cloudflare.com. Those servers receive the phone\'s IP address and the test traffic.\n\nExports are written only where you choose.\n\nQuestions: github.com/mpedreira/nimwifi/issues.</string>
    <string name="precise_location_required_title">Precise location is required for Wi-Fi scanning</string>
    <string name="precise_location_required_message">Android does not allow Wi-Fi scanning with approximate location alone. Open app settings, select Permissions → Location, allow location access while using the app, and enable Use precise location. Return to nimWifi to continue the scan you requested. nimWifi does not request GPS coordinates.</string>
    <string name="open_app_settings">Open app settings</string>
    <string name="app_settings_unavailable">Could not open app settings. Open Android Settings → Apps → nimWifi → Permissions → Location and enable precise location.</string>
